<title>USA: W. House sees FY '97 budget gap under $50 billion.</title>
<headline>W. House sees FY '97 budget gap under $50 billion.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The budget deficit in the current fiscal year ending Sept. 30 looks set to come in at under $50 billion, White House Chief of Staff Erskine Bowles said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The administration ... brought the budget deficit down from $290 billion to less than $50 billion,&quot; he told reporters at a White House briefing on the balanced budget agreement with congressional leaders.</p>
<p>((--Washington Newsroom 202 898-8300))</p>
